Subject: [PATCH 229/230] fix(feed): half-time matches no longer render as live
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The API adapter folds `halftime` into `status: "live"` with
`isHalftime: true` (matchFromApi does the fold so the live sections keep
their bucket), so at runtime `isLive = match.status === "live"` was true
for halftime matches. The `isLive ?` ternary in MatchRow ran first, and
since halftime matches carry no minute label, it rendered the coral
live-dot with no text — visually identical to a live match with no
minute data. The gold `نیمه‌وقت` branch below it was dead code, and the
aria-label said "زنده" instead of the break.

Fix: make `isLive` exclusive of halftime:
  const isLive = match.status === "live" && !isHalftime;

The `isHalftime ?` branch now runs for halftime matches, rendering the
gold label. The `status` label and `aria-label` (which both branch on
`isLive` first) also get the correct value.

Audit finding: audit-full.md, row 1 (HIGH).
File: src/components/LeagueGroup.tsx:89.

